.TH more 1 "FUZIX System Utilities" "FUZIX"
.SH NAME
more \- show a file a screen at a time
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B more
[\fIfile\fR ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B more
prints each
.I file
24 lines at a time, stopping with
.B \-\-More\-\-
at the foot of each screenful.  With several files, each is announced
by its name in angle brackets.
.PP
With no
.IR file ,
it pages standard input.  This is how
.BR man (1)
and anything else that ends in a pipe uses it.
.SH KEYS
At the
.B \-\-More\-\-
prompt:
.TP
.B q
Quit.
.TP
.B n
Go on to the next file, skipping the rest of this one.
.TP
anything else
Show the next screenful.
.PP
A leading colon is ignored, so
.B :q
and
.B :n
work as well.
.SH OPTIONS
None.  There is no search, no backing up, and no line count option.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CTTY
The controlling terminal, which
.B more
must open to read your keypresses when its input is a pipe.
.B init
sets this for every login session.  In a shell that did not come from
.BR init ,
paging a pipe fails with
.BR "more: CTTY not set" .
.SH NOTES
The screen is assumed to be 80 columns by 24 lines, whatever the console
is really set to.  On the 80x40 text console that means it pauses more
often than it needs to.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cat (1),
.BR man (1),
.BR head (1)
